   "module_16049493631818": {
    "body": {
     "hs_enable_module_padding": true,
     "hs_wrapper_css": {
      "padding-bottom": "20px",
      "padding-left": "20px",
      "padding-right": "20px",
      "padding-top": "25px"
     },
     "html": "<p style=\"font-size: 15px; line-height: 150%; text-align: left;\"><span style=\"color: #ffffff; font-family: Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-weight: normal; color: #000000;\">Hi {{ contact.firstname }},</span></span><span style=\"color: #000000;\">&nbsp;</span></p>\n<p>Congratulations on deciding to embark on your journey with your own private label supplement brand!&nbsp;<br><br>If you're like a lot of practitioners or eCommerce entrepreneurs, now you might be feeling somewhat overwhelmed with the logistics. How do you effectively manage shipping? How can you determine the inventory sweet spot and ensure you have enough to avoid going on backorder right away, but not too much to sit on unused inventory?</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>While it might feel daunting, we've put together<span style=\"font-weight: bold;\"> </span><span style=\"color: #6ca439;\"><a href=\"https://www.praxerasupplements.com/blog/managing-private-label-shipping-and-inventory-a-step-by-step-guide\" style=\"font-weight: bold; color: #6ca439;\" rel=\"noopener\">a step-by-step guide to walk you through the process</a><span style=\"font-weight: bold;\">.</span></span></p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p style=\"font-weight: bold;\">In this guide, you'll master the following six steps:</p>\n<ol>\n<li>Partner with a high-quality private label provider</li>\n<li>Choose a fulfillment center</li>\n<li>Discuss inventory and product selection with your provider</li>\n<li>Create your label</li>\n<li>Place your first order</li>\n<li>Track inventory</li>\n</ol>\n<p>Read the entire article for details of how to go about each step. This process will help your private label supplement endeavor be successful from the get-go. Your business and your patients will reap the benefits.</p>",
     "module_id": 1155639
    },
    "child_css": {},
    "css": {},
